+// A browser has no blocking stdin: the bytes of the next message arrive as a
+// JavaScript event, which cannot be delivered while clangd is inside a read.
+// So, before reading a message whose first byte is not already in stdio's
+// buffer, suspend (JSPI) until the embedder has queued at least one whole
+// message. Module.waitForStdin is the embedder's promise for that; it is
+// expected to deliver messages whole, so the reads that follow never find
+// stdin empty in the middle of one.
+EM_ASYNC_JS(void, clangdWaitForStdin, (), {
+  if (Module.waitForStdin) await Module.waitForStdin();
+});
+#endif
